From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:39:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] schema validation: isolate progress OCC from app writes

Stop pending-schema failure and overwrite transactions from reading or deleting the transitioning schema hot progress row. Make the exact active _schemas document and Pending state the ordering fence for every progress initialization and checkpoint, so schema transitions win without weakening serializability.

Clean failed and overwritten progress outside application transactions with read-only discovery and namespace-local exact-key batches. Recheck current schema ownership before reading or deleting progress, and fence cleanup and lifecycle lookups against recreated schema and progress table generations, retained inactive tablets, and reused developer IDs.

Reject simultaneous Pending and Validated schemas throughout submission, overwrite, enforcement, worker and snapshot-import discovery, validation, activation, and active-schema clearing. Deduplicate historical snapshot-import namespaces and add real-committer regressions for race ordering, stale lifecycle and cleanup requests, table recreation, restart cleanup, retention, and dashboard visibility.

Keep exact zero totals visible and retain upstream original-snapshot denominator semantics. Use a one-document minimum checkpoint threshold for an exact zero and the bounded 500-document cadence only when table counts are unavailable.
